data: {"plan":{"aftercare":"Reset the oil maintenance reminder (your owner's manual, Maintenance section), then check the dipstick every few fill-ups. Next change in about 10,000 miles or 12 months.","appliance":"car","brand":"Toyota","diagnosis":"Your 2015 Camry 2.5L is due for fresh oil and a new filter element. It takes 4.6 quarts of 0W-20 with the filter, and the whole job is done from under the front with a drain pan.","library_id":"car-oil-change","library_problem":"engine_oil_due_for_change","manual_url":"https://www.toyota.com/owners/resources/warranty-owners-manuals/camry/2015","model_number":"2015 Camry 2.5L","pro_visit_cost":80,"replacement_parts":["5 quarts of SAE 0W-20 engine oil (it takes 4.6 with the filter)","Toyota oil filter element 04152-YZZA1 with its O-rings","Drain plug gasket, Toyota 90430-12031"],"safety":["Never get under a car held up only by a jack. Use ramps or jack stands, and chock the rear wheels.","Let a hot engine cool about 10 minutes; fresh-off-the-road oil can burn.","Take the old oil and filter to an auto parts store for recycling."],"steps":[{"check":"Both front wheels sit in the ramp cradles and the rear wheels are chocked.","details":["Engine off, parking brake on.","Let a hot engine cool about 10 minutes."],"instruction":"Drive onto ramps, chock the wheels","motion":"none","photo":-1,"show_3d":true,"target_part":"Ramps"},{"check":"The hood is propped and the fill cap is loose.","details":["The release is by your left knee.","Loosening the cap lets the oil drain faster."],"instruction":"Open the hood, loosen the fill cap","motion":"twist_ccw","photo":-1,"show_3d":true,"target_part":"Oil fill cap"},{"check":"The plug is back in with a new gasket and nothing drips.","details":["Turn the plug left, pull it away fast.","Let it drain until it only drips.","Use a new gasket, tighten to 27 ft-lb."],"instruction":"Drain the oil from the 14 mm plug","motion":"unscrew","photo":-1,"show_3d":true,"target_part":"Oil drain plug"},{"check":"The cap is back on snug with the new element inside.","details":["Use the drain tool from the filter box first.","64 mm cap wrench, turn left.","New element and O-ring, oiled. Tighten to 18 ft-lb."],"instruction":"Swap the cartridge filter","motion":"twist_ccw","photo":-1,"show_3d":true,"target_part":"Oil filter (cartridge)"},{"check":"About 4.4 quarts are in and the cap is back on tight.","details":["Use the funnel, go slowly.","Hold the last bit back to check the level first."],"instruction":"Pour in 4.4 quarts of 0W-20","motion":"none","photo":-1,"show_3d":true,"target_part":"Oil fill cap"},{"check":"No drips at the plug or the filter.","details":["Watch the plug and the filter cap.","Engine off, then wait 5 minutes."],"instruction":"Run it one minute, check for drips","motion":"none","photo":-1,"show_3d":true,"target_part":"Oil drain plug"},{"check":"The oil sits between the L and F dots.","details":["Wipe it, push it fully in, pull again.","Add a little at a time if it's below F."],"instruction":"Check the dipstick, top up to F","motion":"pull_out","photo":-1,"show_3d":true,"target_part":"Engine oil dipstick"}],"tools":["Car ramps and wheel chocks","14 mm wrench or socket","64 mm cap-type filter wrench","Drain pan","Funnel","Gloves and rags","Torque wrench (optional)"]},"type":"plan"}

